diagnostics/inheritance-construction.em:37:7: `Needy` needs a constructor, because its field `extra` has no default
  class Needy extends Shape {
        ^^^^^
A class that extends another is built with no arguments unless it has a constructor of its own. Give `extra` a default, or add a constructor that starts with `super(...)` and sets it.
diagnostics/inheritance-construction.em:41:7: `NoFields` needs a constructor, because building `Shape` takes arguments
  class NoFields extends Shape {
